-- title:
--   Pull-back of even rigidified pairs with transported Deligne datum
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $r\neq\bar r$ are primes and $N\neq 0$ is squarefree and divisible by neither (`hrr`, `hrN`, `hrbarN`, `hN`).
--
--   **Coefficients.** $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), $\pi$ an irreducible element, $\mathcal O$ is $\pi$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), $\#(\mathcal O/\pi)=r$ (`hres`) and $(r)=(\pi)$ (`hunr`); $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero field realised as the fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Next, $Onr$ is a characteristic-zero domain over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-automorphism $Fr$, complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), that ideal being maximal (`hOnr_max`), every element of $Onr$ satisfying a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial of positive degree over $Onr$ having a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $Fr(x)\equiv x^r \pmod \pi$ (`hFr`). A homomorphism $vdet:\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) is characterised by `hvdet`: $vdet(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g$ is a unit of $\mathcal O$ times $\pi^n$.
--
--   **Indefinite side and moduli.** $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ is indefinite and ramified exactly at $r$ and $\bar r$ (`hB`), with maximal order $\Lambda$ (`hΛ`) containing $\mathbb Z$ (`hΛℤ`). A scheme $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point assignment $pt$ is a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure (`h𝒳`); for $n\geq 3$ prime to $r$, $\bar r$ and $N$, $M$ with $ptF$ is a fine moduli space for such curves with full level-$n$ structure (`hM`), carrying a level-twisting action of a group $G$ through $\rho:G\to\operatorname{Aut}M$ with labels $\chi:G\to\Lambda$ (`hρ`); $p:M\to\mathcal X$ lies over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ (`hp`), is $G$-invariant (`hρp`) and forgets the level-$n$ structure on points (`hp_pt`). For every prime $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$, $\mathcal Y_\ell$ with $ptT_\ell$ is a coarse moduli space for curves with extra level-$\ell$ structure (`h𝒴`), and the degeneracy maps $d_0,d_1$ lie over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) and compute, on points, the underlying curve and its $\ell$-isogenous quotient (`hd₀`, `hd₁`). Finally $ar,arbar:\mathcal X\to\mathcal X$ lie over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ (`harf`, `harbarf`) and realise the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **Definite side.** $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ is definite and ramified exactly at $\bar r$ (`hdef`), with maximal order $\Lambda_1$, an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ contained in $\Lambda_1$ (`hΛ₁`, `hR₁`, `hRΛ₁`), an idele $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ (`hn₁`) such that $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`), an injective $\mathbb Q$-embedding $\iota_0$ into $M_2(K_0)$ (`hι₀`), and a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ above $r$ (`hv`). The group $\Gamma t$ consists of the units integral away from $v$ for $R_1$ (`hΓt`); families $s_\ell$, $sf_\ell$ satisfy `hs` (four clauses: $sf_\ell$ is the image of $s_\ell$ away from $r$, is $1$ at $r$, the diagonal idele of $\ell$ times $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in the level Hecke set of $(\Lambda_1,R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1})$ at $\ell$ if $\ell\mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$), and $\Gamma t_\ell=\Gamma t\cap s_\ell\,\Gamma t\,s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`); $\bar w$ is a unit of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma t$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   **Data on the special fibre.** $coord$ is an order coordinate map $\Lambda\to \mathbb Z_{p^2}(r)^2$ (`hcoord`); $A_0$ is a fake elliptic curve over $Onr/(\pi)$, $X_0$ a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over that ring of height $4$ (`hX₀`), $\theta_0$ a system of two-dimensional formal coordinates for $A_0$, and $A_0$ is a formal module via $coord$, $X_0$, $\theta_0$ (`hA₀`). Endomorphism families $e,e':\Gamma t\to\operatorname{End}(A_0.A)$ over the base (`he`) with degrees $deg$ satisfy the groups `hE1` (isogeny pairs of degree $r^{deg\gamma}$ preserving the level structure), `hE1mul`, `hE1sc` (multiplicativity and scalars, each up to multiplication by powers of $r$), `hE1'` (only scalar $\gamma$ give scalar $e\gamma$ up to powers of $r$), `hE2` (for every injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $X_0$-endomorphisms into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $e\gamma$ is induced on formal coordinates by a central element $\varepsilon$ with $E_0\varepsilon=r^{k_\gamma}\,g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$), `hE3` (labelling of the action on a full level-$n$ structure by elements of $\Lambda$, multiplicative and compatible with scalars modulo $n$) and `hE4` (on geometric fibres, every level-preserving $r$-power isogeny comes from some $\gamma\in\Gamma t$ up to powers of $r$). An order $R_2\leq R_1$ with $r$-power denominators (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`, `hR₂r`) carries $\hat e:R_2\to\operatorname{End}(A_0.A)$ over the base (`hê`) subject to `hE5a` (additivity, commutation with the $\Lambda$-action, preservation of the level structure), `hE5b1`–`hE5b3` (unit, products, integers), `hE5c` (norms), `hE5d` (agreement with $e$ up to powers of $r$) and `hE5e` (the matching of `hE2` extended simultaneously to $R_2$). A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$ is given, together with an Atkin–Lehner datum at $\bar r$ over the special fibre: $A_{0w}$, $aw$, $aw'$, $bw$, $bw'$, $k_w$ with `hALw` (Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ via $aw$, $aw'$), `hBSw` (isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$), `hBSwlev` (preservation of level) and `hJOINTw` (the matching of `hE2` extended to the composite $aw$ followed by $bw$, which corresponds to $\bar w$).
--
--   **Formal moduli and the Drinfeld comparison.** $\iota:\mathbb Z_{p^2}(r)\to Onr$ is a ring map, $\Phi$ a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $Onr/(r)$ which is special for the induced structure map (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`); $MD$ is a moduli package for $r$ over $Onr$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`), and $\eta$ attaches to each rigidified object over a base with $r$ nilpotent a point of $MD$, subject to `hη` (three clauses: $\eta$ separates admissible rigidified objects exactly up to isomorphism, is natural in the base, and is surjective after a Zariski cover). The map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the endomorphisms of $\Phi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ is injective and has image commensurable with $M_2(\mathcal O)$ in the precise sense of `hE₀`. The family $eD$ compares the functor of $MD$-points with the product of the functor corepresented by $Onr$ and Deligne's functor $\Omega$ of lines in lattice base changes: it is natural (`hnatD`), bijective (`hbijD`), has first component the structural map $\psi$ (`hfstD`), intertwines the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action on $MD$-points with the twisted action on $\Omega$-data (`hGLD`), sends $\pi$-translates to the Frobenius twist of the first component with unchanged datum (`hPiD`), and $\pi$-translates always exist (`hPiexD`). Further, $\kappa:Onr/(\pi)\to Onr/(r)$ is compatible with the quotient maps (`hκ`), and $\beta_0$ is an isogeny of height $4n_0$ from $\Phi$ to the reduction of $X_0$ along $\kappa$ (`hβ₀`).
--
--   **The classifying map $\Xi$.** $\Xi$ assigns to every rigidified curve over a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, with structural map $\psi:Onr\to B$, a point of the $MD$-functor; it satisfies `hΞleg` (over a $B$ with only trivial idempotents the leg of $\Xi$ is some integral Frobenius twist of $\psi$), `hΞnat` (compatibility with pull-back of curves and rigidifications), `hΞiso` (invariance under isomorphisms of curves compatible with the group law, the $\Lambda$-action and the level structure, whose rigidifications are comparable in the stated sense) and `hΞdef` (over such a $B$ with $r$ nilpotent, for a rigidified curve carrying a formal module structure via $coord$ there are $j\leq 1$ and a rigidified object $t$ with $t.X$ the given formal module, transported from $\theta_0$ through $\kappa$ and $\beta_0$ with exponent $j$, admissible for $\iota$ and $\psi\circ Fr^{-j}$, such that $\Xi$ of the curve is the point $\eta(t)$ with leg $\psi\circ Fr^{-j}$). Finally $g_0\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ is such that translating a rigidification by $e\gamma$ moves $\Xi$ by the action of a power of the scalar $r$ times $g_0\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g_0^{-1}$ (`heqΓ`), and passing to the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ moves $\Xi$ by a power of the scalar $r$ times $g_0\,\iota_0(\bar w)\,g_0^{-1}$ (`heqW`), both over bases with only trivial idempotents.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Write $\psi^{\circ}:=\psi\circ Fr^{-vdet(g_0)}$ for the Frobenius twist of $\psi$ by $-vdet(g_0)$. The assertion is: for all Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ and $B'$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\varphi:B\to B'$, every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi:Onr\to B$, every Deligne datum $P$ over $B$, every fake elliptic curve $E$ over $B$ with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure, and every rigidification $\varrho$ of $E$ relative to $A_0$ along $\psi^{\circ}$, if
--
--   (i) the leg of $\Xi(E,\varrho)$ over $\psi^{\circ}$ equals $\psi^{\circ}$, and
--
--   (ii) $eD(\Xi(E,\varrho))$ is carried to the pair $(\psi,P)$ by the twisted action of $g_0^{-1}$, that is: $\psi$ is the Frobenius twist of the first component of $eD(\Xi(E,\varrho))$ by $vdet(g_0)$, and for every full lattice $M$ the line $P(M)$ is the preimage, under the base-changed action of $g_0$, of the line of the second component at $g_0\cdot M$,
--
--   then there exist a fake elliptic curve $E'$ over $B'$ with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure, a morphism $g:E'.A\to E.A$ exhibiting $E'$ as the pull-back of $E$ along $\varphi$ (a pull-back square over $\operatorname{Spec}\varphi$, compatible with the group laws, with the $\Lambda$-actions, and carrying sections factoring through the level structure of $E'$ to sections factoring through that of $E$), and a rigidification $\varrho'$ of $E'$ along $\varphi\circ\psi^{\circ}$, such that:
--
--   (a) $\varrho'$ is the pull-back of $\varrho$ along $\varphi$ and $g$: there are maps $ub$, $uA$ exhibiting the reductions modulo $\pi$ of the curve and of the auxiliary curve of $\varrho'$ as pull-backs of those of $\varrho$ along the induced map of quotients, with $ub$ followed by $\varrho.gb$ equal to $\varrho'.gb$ followed by $g$, with $uA$ followed by $\varrho.gA$ equal to $\varrho'.gA$, with equal isogeny exponents, and with $ub$ followed by $\varrho.\varphi$ equal to $\varrho'.\varphi$ followed by $uA$;
--
--   (b) the leg of $\Xi(E',\varrho')$ over $\varphi\circ\psi^{\circ}$ equals $\varphi\circ\psi^{\circ}$; and
--
--   (c) $eD(\Xi(E',\varrho'))$ is carried to the pair $(\varphi\circ\psi,\ \Omega(\varphi)(P))$ by the twisted action of $g_0^{-1}$, in the same sense as in (ii).
--
--   No hypothesis of connectedness, nor of nilpotence of $r$, is imposed on $B$ or $B'$ in the conclusion.
--
--   This is the pull-back clause of the axiomatic frame for the Čerednik–Drinfeld description of the fake elliptic curve moduli problem over a complete discretely valued base: it says that the subfunctor of rigidified pairs which are "even" (untwisted leg) with prescribed Deligne datum is stable under base change of the coefficient algebra, the datum being transported by $\Omega(\varphi)$. It feeds the uniqueness-and-existence statement for pull-back lifts of even rigidified pairs and, through it, the construction of the fine and coarse tower families over the Čerednik–Drinfeld base.
